course: dictionary
lesson: 8382
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word rubber can mean a soft, stretchy material, or a small block for rubbing out pencil marks. «The grooves in a tyre's tread push water away so the rubber can grip.» Here rubber is the stretchy material, because a tyre grips the road, and not something you use on paper.
explain: Look at the words around the word. In «Please pass me the rubber, I made a mistake», a rubber is something you use to fix writing. In the UK, Ireland and Australia that is what people mean, while in the USA they say eraser. Try your meaning in the sentence: does it still make sense?
explain: Rubber can also mean things made of rubber, such as boots, gloves and balls. Rubber boots are also called wellies. Rubber soles on shoes grip the ground and stop you slipping.
fact: Rubber is a soft, stretchy material that bounces and keeps water out.
fact: Rubber comes from the sap of rubber trees, or it can be made from chemicals.
fact: In the UK, Ireland and Australia, a rubber is a small block for rubbing out pencil marks; in the USA this is called an eraser.
fact: Rubber does not let electricity pass through it easily, so it is used on electricians' tools and on the handles of some tools.
fact: «Metals let electricity flow because they have loose electrons that can drift along; plastic, rubber and wood block it.»
exercise: «The grooves in a tyre's tread push water away so the rubber can grip.» What does rubber mean here? | *A soft, stretchy material used for tyres | A rubber duck in the bath | A tiny pencil case | An eraser for pencil marks
exercise: «Metals let electricity flow because they have loose electrons that can drift along; plastic, rubber and wood block it.» Which material blocks electricity? | Iron | Copper | Silver | *Rubber
exercise: In the UK, Australia and Ireland, what is a rubber? | A car tyre | A piece of chewing gum | A pencil case | *A small block for rubbing out pencil marks
test: What are rubber boots also called? | Sandals | *Wellies | Slippers | Trainers
test: Rubber can mean things made of rubber. Which of these is one of them? | Sand | *Tyres | Ice | Rain
exam: Why do tools for electricians have rubber handles? | *Because rubber does not let electricity pass through it easily | Because rubber is heavy and stops tools falling | Because rubber smells of flowers | Because rubber is shiny and looks nice
